{
  "profile": "room",
  "profile_page": "profiles/room.md",
  "notes": [
    "pairs: the ten type-and-supertype pairs a reader matches, each trimmed and compared without regard to case. The order is the table's and carries no meaning: a reader matches a pair and may keep them as a set. A serial never reorders the pairs that exist; a new pair goes where the page's table puts it, and the release notes name its place; so a suite that pins the order turns red only when a pair is added.",
    "mark: x_room_of, the id of the world or the sitting the room belongs to; a room element carries it, a lore element never does.",
    "item: x_room_item, written only on a Take, the id of the work item the take is on; it makes nothing a room element, the pair and the mark do.",
    "cases: element gives type, supertype and x_room_of as a body might carry them, or is a value that is not an object (null, a list, a string), which is no room element; in_room is what isRoomElement must answer: the pair AND the mark. A case's note, where one is given, is prose for the reader of the fixture, never an input.",
    "talk_cases: each element is a Narrative as a body carries it, with its links; only a line in the room (the pair narrative + Message and the mark) is in a talk on an element, so any other element (a Message without the mark, a board entry) is in none; talks is every talk on an element the line is in, each {type, id}: an id in objects as object, an id in constructs as construct, read from the line alone, compared as a set; an entry that is not a string, or is empty once trimmed of White_Space (the room profile's set), names no element, a field that is not a list names none, and every other entry is an id read as written, a space left on it included, never folded to lowercase. No other field puts a line in a talk on an element: characters are its recipients, and a work item it hangs on (the report profile's anchor) is no talk on an element."
  ],
